WEBVTT

00:00:02.030 --> 00:00:04.050
<i>In his search for clues 
to locate Radiant,</i>

00:00:04.050 --> 00:00:09.220
<i>Seth is heading to the ancient city
 of sorcerers, Caislean Merlin.</i>

00:00:09.220 --> 00:00:13.510
<i>Meanwhile, Dragunov,
 who has just become a Thaumaturge,</i>

00:00:13.510 --> 00:00:18.030
<i>is pursuing Seth, whom the Inquisition 
perceives to be a serious threat.</i>

00:00:18.810 --> 00:00:22.060
<i>Seth's destination is
 where his new adventure begins:</i>

00:00:22.060 --> 00:00:24.000
<i>the continent of Cyfandir.</i>

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:27.000
Listen up, Seth.

00:00:27.350 --> 00:00:30.470
This is where we are right now.

00:00:30.890 --> 00:00:32.970
Once you land on the continent 
and leave the forest,

00:00:32.970 --> 00:00:34.870
you'll be in Caislean Merlin.

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:37.550
Make sure you walk there.

00:00:38.250 --> 00:00:40.880
I can't fly in on my broom?

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:44.290
If you want the Inquisitors
 to catch you, be my guest.

00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:47.020
They've got their eyes on you, remember?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.590
R-Right...

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:50.570
Yo, Seth!

00:00:49.400 --> 00:00:50.570
What the heck?!

00:00:50.570 --> 00:00:53.140
Here are some parting gifts from us!

00:00:53.140 --> 00:00:54.830
It's food and a broom.

00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:57.070
Use this to fly as far as Cyfandir.

00:00:57.070 --> 00:00:59.230
Hey, thanks!

00:00:59.230 --> 00:01:00.590
Wait, it's too short!

00:01:00.590 --> 00:01:02.900
That's only half a broom!

00:01:03.870 --> 00:01:05.810
Well, I got it for half price!

00:01:06.830 --> 00:01:10.290
What's the problem?
 If the broom flies, ride it!

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:16.060
I still think it's gonna 
be too hard to ride this.

00:01:16.060 --> 00:01:19.050
You're young.
 You'll get the hang of it in no time.

00:01:19.050 --> 00:01:21.770
Don't fall off before
 you get to the continent.

00:01:21.770 --> 00:01:23.350
R-Right!

00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:27.100
I'll stay in touch this time.
 I promise.

00:01:27.100 --> 00:01:29.670
Yeah, sure. Do what you want.

00:01:30.370 --> 00:01:32.330
Take care, now!

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.110
Seth!

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:48.370
So that's the continent of Cyfandir?

00:03:20.880 --> 00:03:26.890
<b>An Encounter in the Rain 
-Mist-</b>

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.940
<i>"An Encounter in the Rain."</i>

00:03:30.670 --> 00:03:32.900
There you are, sir.

00:03:33.470 --> 00:03:37.150
As planned, we should 
arrive in Bome within a day,

00:03:37.150 --> 00:03:40.380
Vice Captain—I mean, Captain Goudeau.

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.330
Fine.
 And you can still call me "Vice Captain."

00:03:44.330 --> 00:03:46.780
We haven't received official notice
 about the change yet.

00:03:46.780 --> 00:03:50.040
Besides, Captain Dragunov 
is our true captain.

00:03:51.450 --> 00:03:52.150
Yes, sir!

00:03:53.390 --> 00:04:01.180
But... so many of our forces have been called
 to the home base at Bome.

00:04:01.180 --> 00:04:03.180
Is a major operation in the works?

00:04:03.180 --> 00:04:05.010
I couldn't say.

00:04:05.010 --> 00:04:07.800
But Bome is not a monolith.

00:04:07.800 --> 00:04:11.060
There's no telling
 what schemes may be at work there.

00:04:12.750 --> 00:04:16.210
Where could Captain Dragunov 
be at a time like this?

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:24.070
I didn't think we'd be sent on a mission
 without any of our men.

00:04:25.420 --> 00:04:30.330
And sending two Thaumaturges so far away
 just to chase down a child?

00:04:30.330 --> 00:04:33.830
That just tells you
 how fixated the general is

00:04:34.300 --> 00:04:36.210
on this horned boy.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:40.370
He's already long gone from Artemis.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:42.720
The next place he'll go...

00:04:42.720 --> 00:04:45.490
...must be Cyfandir.

00:04:45.490 --> 00:04:46.600
Yes.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:50.850
The nation of Knights-sorcerers
 that's caused so much trouble for us.

00:04:55.970 --> 00:04:57.980
You like drinking with a straw, huh?

00:04:58.850 --> 00:05:01.230
It's my style. Always has been.

00:05:01.230 --> 00:05:05.670
I know that.
 I served under you, after all.

00:05:05.670 --> 00:05:07.240
I guess so.

00:05:07.240 --> 00:05:11.990
So I know how you think 
better than most.

00:05:14.220 --> 00:05:16.690
When you have that look in your eyes,

00:05:16.690 --> 00:05:19.550
you're thinking of doing something 
that deviates from your orders.

00:05:20.450 --> 00:05:21.630
Am I wrong?

00:05:24.010 --> 00:05:28.120
Oh, please. I'm a Thaumaturge now.

00:05:28.120 --> 00:05:31.570
I'm not some lowly captain
 who can get away with mischief.

00:05:31.570 --> 00:05:33.270
But before any of that,

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:36.520
you're Dart Dragunov.

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:40.330
Even I think
 I've grown up a <i>little</i> bit.

00:05:40.870 --> 00:05:42.400
The only dreamer we need

00:05:42.750 --> 00:05:47.780
is that kid who insists
 that he's actually looking for Radiant.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:57.010
<i>So, kid...</i>

00:05:57.010 --> 00:06:00.420
<i>Where are you now,
 and what are you doing?</i>

00:06:07.240 --> 00:06:10.930
<b>Continent of Cyfandir</b>

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.680
I can barely even move forward
 in this rain.

00:06:15.010 --> 00:06:17.420
Come on, move! Move!

00:06:31.780 --> 00:06:34.300
Did you guys just hear a "thunk"?

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.700
Probably just a bird
 flying into the ship again.

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:39.630
The poor bird...

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:41.370
We're preparing to land!

00:06:41.370 --> 00:06:44.730
Dispatch the Barons' small craft at once!

00:06:44.730 --> 00:06:46.340
Y-Yes, sir!

00:06:46.340 --> 00:06:49.590
My broom... My food...

00:06:49.590 --> 00:06:51.660
I-I'm slipping!

00:06:56.790 --> 00:06:57.870
Is that...

00:07:02.410 --> 00:07:05.020
Did you guys just hear a "boing"?

00:07:05.020 --> 00:07:06.480
Again?

00:07:07.060 --> 00:07:09.090
All these weird noises, and this fog...

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:10.940
I hate to think about
 what we're heading into.

00:07:10.940 --> 00:07:13.370
Darling, did you hear?

00:07:13.370 --> 00:07:16.490
There are rumors that ghosts
 have been seen in this area.

00:07:16.620 --> 00:07:18.120
What?

00:07:18.120 --> 00:07:21.830
Wh-What will we do
 if there really are ghosts?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:26.420
Honestly...
 Why did I marry such a coward?

00:07:26.420 --> 00:07:28.380
Huh? What did you say?

00:07:28.380 --> 00:07:31.340
Ghosts? Fantastic!

00:07:31.340 --> 00:07:34.410
I'd love to add one to my collection.

00:07:34.410 --> 00:07:37.890
Hey, Cristolom,
 would you catch one for me?

00:07:38.590 --> 00:07:40.140
Foolishness!

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:42.140
There's no such thing!

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:45.360
Th-Then maybe it's the Knights-sorcerers!

00:07:45.360 --> 00:07:47.490
This is their domain, isn't it?

00:07:47.490 --> 00:07:50.530
No, no. Everything will be fine.

00:07:50.940 --> 00:07:53.530
They've been our friends 
for a long time.

00:07:53.530 --> 00:07:56.860
We're visiting only as part of our vacation.

00:07:56.860 --> 00:07:59.790
They wouldn't just attack us
 without warning.

00:07:59.790 --> 00:08:05.540
Oh? You didn't bring us along 
just for a picnic, did you?

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.880
Of course not.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:12.270
Everything we do is for the purpose
 of earning big profits.

00:08:12.270 --> 00:08:16.180
That is the way of the Merchant Barons.

00:08:16.180 --> 00:08:18.030
<i>The Merchant Barons.</i>

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:22.330
<i>To them, discrimination against 
the infected and the Nemesis calamity</i>

00:08:22.330 --> 00:08:24.450
<i>are merely more opportunities 
to make money.</i>

00:08:24.980 --> 00:08:27.130
<i>Behind the scenes of every conflict,</i>

00:08:27.130 --> 00:08:31.190
<i>one is sure to find
 these greedy merchants of death.</i>

00:08:32.140 --> 00:08:33.820
So cold...

00:08:42.490 --> 00:08:45.290
What fantastic natural resources!

00:08:45.290 --> 00:08:49.380
Encountering a new fortune 
is such a euphoric feeling!

00:08:50.210 --> 00:08:52.700
I wish I could encounter someone new.

00:08:52.700 --> 00:08:54.590
Huh? What did you say?

00:08:54.590 --> 00:08:56.540
Behold, gentlemen.

00:08:56.540 --> 00:08:58.830
If we can have our way with this land,

00:08:58.830 --> 00:09:01.580
we can surely generate immense profits.

00:09:01.580 --> 00:09:05.730
B-But... doesn't this land 
belong to Caislean Merlin?

00:09:07.410 --> 00:09:09.320
Yes... for now.

00:09:09.320 --> 00:09:14.500
Besides, this continent is home to resources
 far more valuable than this land.

00:09:14.500 --> 00:09:17.110
Baron Doussant, do you mean...

00:09:19.120 --> 00:09:22.540
Hey! Anyone find that rock yet?

00:09:22.540 --> 00:09:26.170
No. You can be the first to find it.

00:09:26.170 --> 00:09:28.630
Oh? Well, I appreciate that!

00:09:31.930 --> 00:09:33.880
If I can get over to that branch...

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:37.010
Okay, here I go!

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.740
Ouch!

00:09:42.740 --> 00:09:46.100
Oh, dear.
 I'll have to have them patched up.

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:48.100
If only we lived in the days
 of my ancestors,

00:09:48.100 --> 00:09:51.450
when I could just swap them out
 for new slaves...

00:09:51.450 --> 00:09:53.200
Pazz! Your belly!

00:09:53.200 --> 00:09:58.650
Yes, perhaps eating six chickens
 was a bit too much,

00:09:58.650 --> 00:10:00.970
but I really wanted them—

00:09:59.660 --> 00:10:02.910
No! Something's stuck in your belly!

00:10:07.830 --> 00:10:10.340
Oh! It's a little goat boy!

00:10:10.340 --> 00:10:12.170
I want him for my collection!

00:10:12.170 --> 00:10:15.090
No, those horns... He's an infected!

00:10:16.010 --> 00:10:18.180
One of the Knights-sorcerers?!

00:10:18.180 --> 00:10:19.930
Take up your weapons!

00:10:20.910 --> 00:10:24.180
Wait, wait, wait!
 I'm not a Knight-sorcerer!

00:10:24.180 --> 00:10:26.940
No? Then who are you?

00:10:26.940 --> 00:10:30.610
I was flying and 
I crashed into your airship!

00:10:30.610 --> 00:10:33.070
My broom broke,
 so I had to hang on for dear life!

00:10:33.070 --> 00:10:36.320
All lies! He's definitely a spy!

00:10:36.320 --> 00:10:39.500
You! Whom are you spying for?

00:10:39.500 --> 00:10:41.600
I'm not spying!

00:10:41.600 --> 00:10:44.450
Maybe you'll tell the truth 
if I rough you up a little!

00:10:45.070 --> 00:10:48.210
You guys just don't listen, do you?!

00:10:54.330 --> 00:10:55.460
He ran off!

00:10:56.140 --> 00:10:57.060
After him!

00:10:57.060 --> 00:10:58.970
I don't have time for this!

00:10:58.970 --> 00:11:00.490
There may be more like him!

00:11:00.490 --> 00:11:03.220
Protect the Merchant Barons!

00:11:03.560 --> 00:11:06.010
Come, Vigilant! 
We're hunting an infected!

00:11:06.970 --> 00:11:08.860
No! No! No!

00:11:08.860 --> 00:11:11.380
The goat boy belongs to me!

00:11:11.380 --> 00:11:14.230
Cristolom, bring him back alive!

00:11:14.230 --> 00:11:16.820
No way. Too much trouble.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.620
Come on, please!

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:22.660
I'll give you my vineyard in Malsudant
 and my barren land in Mauve!

00:11:22.660 --> 00:11:23.470
Nope.

00:11:23.470 --> 00:11:26.980
I'll throw in two hills 
and three castles!

00:11:27.790 --> 00:11:29.820
Well, in that case, I'll do it.

00:11:30.540 --> 00:11:32.870
I'm glad that deal came so cheap.

00:11:40.810 --> 00:11:44.260
I guess it's time for a little warm-up.

00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:48.110
After him!

00:11:48.110 --> 00:11:49.270
Get him!

00:11:49.610 --> 00:11:51.890
I have no broom and
 I don't know the terrain.

00:11:51.890 --> 00:11:53.660
I need to lose them somehow!

00:11:56.050 --> 00:11:57.520
After him!

00:11:57.520 --> 00:11:59.410
Don't let him get away!

00:12:00.530 --> 00:12:02.740
All right! It worked!

00:12:09.430 --> 00:12:11.160
Something's stuck in me!

00:12:19.090 --> 00:12:23.530
Oh, I get it.
 That bird's telling them where I am.

00:12:23.530 --> 00:12:24.970
In that case...

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:28.470
Titan Punch!

00:12:30.470 --> 00:12:32.100
There you are.

00:12:37.660 --> 00:12:41.280
My legs are far stronger 
than any ordinary man's.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:44.740
Now, let us stuff you and
 mount your corpse, Knight-sorcerer!

00:12:44.740 --> 00:12:47.860
I told you, I'm not a Knight-sorcerer!

00:12:47.860 --> 00:12:51.470
Skull Attack!

00:12:57.630 --> 00:13:01.090
That kind of magic can't touch me!

00:13:01.090 --> 00:13:02.840
It didn't work?!

00:13:05.510 --> 00:13:07.590
Those legs can't be legal!

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.570
I'll hear no complaints!

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:11.350
Needle Rain!

00:13:11.940 --> 00:13:13.730
Repulse!

00:13:15.650 --> 00:13:17.480
Damn you! Damn you!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:19.580
White silver?!

00:13:17.480 --> 00:13:21.170
Damn you! Damn you!

00:13:23.280 --> 00:13:24.200
Now then...

00:13:26.020 --> 00:13:28.620
I'm sure he fell somewhere around here.

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:32.060
I am, and will always be, the Great Finder!

00:13:32.060 --> 00:13:35.420
I can find anything,
 no matter where it's hiding!

00:13:36.690 --> 00:13:37.870
There you are!

00:13:42.700 --> 00:13:43.630
What?!

00:13:43.630 --> 00:13:45.030
Baron!

00:13:47.070 --> 00:13:49.760
Gh-Ghosts!

00:13:49.760 --> 00:13:51.760
R-Retreat!

00:14:02.020 --> 00:14:08.030
<b>[Vino Divino] 
Baron Cristolom's beloved fortifying medicine.
 It is produced by the Merchant Barons,
 but some say a certain member of
 the Inquisition used to drink it...</b>

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.870
<i>What's... going on?</i>

00:14:28.050 --> 00:14:29.170
<i>What...</i>

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:35.130
<i>You're...</i>

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.740
You've finally returned
 to the land of the living.

00:14:51.570 --> 00:14:54.740
Grimm? What are you doing here?

00:14:55.980 --> 00:14:58.970
Did you save me from those guys?

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:00.310
Indeed.

00:15:00.310 --> 00:15:04.750
Grimm knows many ways to evade enemies
 without fighting them.

00:15:04.750 --> 00:15:08.620
You're amazing.
 I should learn from you.

00:15:08.620 --> 00:15:10.270
Wise.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:14.450
But you have Fantasia. 
Why did you not use it?

00:15:14.450 --> 00:15:15.140
Huh?

00:15:15.490 --> 00:15:19.900
With your power,
 you could have gotten out of that on your own.

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:21.900
Well...

00:15:28.510 --> 00:15:30.650
I'd rather not use it 
if I don't have to.

00:15:33.650 --> 00:15:38.690
The fight at Rumble Town came way too close
 to becoming a huge disaster.

00:15:38.690 --> 00:15:41.670
Well, I suppose that is fortunate.

00:15:41.670 --> 00:15:43.420
How is that fortunate?

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:49.570
You didn't have to bear the burden 
of many hundreds of deaths.

00:15:50.270 --> 00:15:52.300
And you know that burden?

00:16:00.620 --> 00:16:01.940
Grimm?

00:16:02.530 --> 00:16:06.690
It's getting late.
 You should wait until morning to leave.

00:16:07.100 --> 00:16:08.970
Grimm cast a spell
 to close your wounds,

00:16:08.970 --> 00:16:11.950
but you should still rest 
 for a bit longer.

00:16:11.950 --> 00:16:13.590
Okay. Thanks.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:16.200
But that was pretty low, Grimm.

00:16:17.940 --> 00:16:22.400
You were watching over me 
from a distance, right?

00:16:22.400 --> 00:16:25.080
Why didn't you tell me sooner 
that you were there?

00:16:25.080 --> 00:16:28.290
Why did you come here alone?

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:31.020
Why not let your friends know?

00:16:31.020 --> 00:16:36.410
Because... I didn't want them to get 
 into trouble because of me.

00:16:39.010 --> 00:16:41.050
The same goes for Grimm.

00:16:46.780 --> 00:16:48.830
Darn it!

00:16:48.830 --> 00:16:53.850
Why didn't you catch my goat boy for me?

00:16:53.850 --> 00:16:55.740
Don't throw a tantrum!

00:16:55.740 --> 00:16:58.200
We were attacked by enemies 
we didn't expect!

00:16:58.200 --> 00:17:01.490
They seemed almost like ghosts.

00:17:01.490 --> 00:17:05.450
H-Hey, shouldn't we go back home now?

00:17:05.450 --> 00:17:07.470
Ghosts are scary!

00:17:07.470 --> 00:17:08.970
Coward.

00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:09.750
Huh?

00:17:09.750 --> 00:17:14.130
If I can't add to my collection,
 I want to go home!

00:17:16.210 --> 00:17:18.140
Have you gentlemen forgotten?

00:17:18.860 --> 00:17:24.220
We lost a crucial production base
 in the Rumble Town riots.

00:17:24.220 --> 00:17:28.150
Did I not explain that we need
 a new source of income?

00:17:28.150 --> 00:17:29.810
That's true, but...

00:17:29.810 --> 00:17:34.150
Don't talk about that!
 You'll make me lose my appetite!

00:17:34.150 --> 00:17:37.420
While it may be true
 that we have other bases,

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:40.610
the loss of the weapons we were 
selling to the Inquisition

00:17:40.610 --> 00:17:43.160
has caused a drop in our profits.

00:17:43.160 --> 00:17:44.450
Exactly.

00:17:44.450 --> 00:17:45.960
The Inquisition was working with us,

00:17:45.960 --> 00:17:49.080
and now that their authority has plummeted,

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:51.750
our voices are less influential, as well.

00:17:52.230 --> 00:17:58.180
Still, was it really necessary for us
 to come to this continent in person?

00:17:58.180 --> 00:18:01.410
Listen to me.
 They say the incident in Rumble Town

00:18:01.410 --> 00:18:05.310
was caused entirely
 by just a handful of sorcerers.

00:18:06.090 --> 00:18:10.150
That incident changed the world,
 without a doubt.

00:18:10.150 --> 00:18:11.810
There were already factors at work

00:18:11.810 --> 00:18:15.270
to change the world in places 
we didn't even know existed.

00:18:16.360 --> 00:18:21.180
The world is about to see another 
colossal change in Caislean Merlin.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:25.060
And this time,
 we must be there at any cost.

00:18:25.060 --> 00:18:27.770
How do you know that's going to happen?

00:18:29.180 --> 00:18:31.030
You'll find out in time.

00:18:31.030 --> 00:18:33.000
Tell me just one thing.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:34.570
Does this have to do with

00:18:34.570 --> 00:18:38.320
the resource more valuable than this land
 you spoke of earlier?

00:18:38.320 --> 00:18:39.860
It does.

00:18:39.860 --> 00:18:44.430
It's something that will 
bring us a shining future.

00:18:55.670 --> 00:18:58.170
Just follow this path,

00:18:58.170 --> 00:19:00.810
and you will reach the castle
 of Caislean Merlin.

00:19:03.470 --> 00:19:05.690
Thanks for everything, Grimm.

00:19:05.690 --> 00:19:07.990
You're actually good
 at looking out for others, huh?

00:19:08.950 --> 00:19:11.460
No one has ever said that
 to Grimm before.

00:19:12.960 --> 00:19:17.510
That aside, take care 
not to stray from this path.

00:19:18.530 --> 00:19:21.140
The castle is surrounded 
by powerful magic

00:19:21.140 --> 00:19:23.720
that confuses one's sense of direction.

00:19:23.720 --> 00:19:25.660
If you wander into its vicinity carelessly,

00:19:25.660 --> 00:19:27.970
you will be lost for months.

00:19:30.060 --> 00:19:32.660
You sure know a lot about this place.

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:35.510
Grimm?

00:19:36.210 --> 00:19:38.250
He left without even saying goodbye?

00:19:38.250 --> 00:19:41.360
Why's he even on this continent, anyway?

00:19:42.950 --> 00:19:44.540
Oh, well.

00:19:45.610 --> 00:19:47.590
I'm sure I'll see him again eventually.

00:20:11.620 --> 00:20:16.270
<b>Caislean Merlin</b>

00:20:17.230 --> 00:20:19.280
Wow...

00:20:19.680 --> 00:20:21.700
It's huge!

00:20:21.700 --> 00:20:24.580
So this is the castle of the Knights-sorcerers?

00:20:27.210 --> 00:20:28.770
Wait up!

00:20:28.770 --> 00:20:31.290
Hey, Nemesis!
 The Knights-sorcerers will take you on!

00:20:32.790 --> 00:20:36.500
I'm tired of playing the 
Nemesis all the time!

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.340
I wanna be a Knight-sorcerer!

00:20:38.340 --> 00:20:42.490
But you have to do it.
 Your curse makes you stand out.

00:20:42.490 --> 00:20:44.330
Why does that matter? It's just a game!

00:20:44.330 --> 00:20:47.650
Okay, fine.
 But only if you can catch us.

00:20:47.650 --> 00:20:48.430
Okay!

00:20:48.430 --> 00:20:50.340
All right, here I come!

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:52.250
Oh, no! It's a Nemesis!

00:20:52.250 --> 00:20:54.440
Hey! Wait up!

00:21:15.830 --> 00:21:19.010
<i>People who are cursed are getting along</i>

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:20.500
<i>with people who aren't?</i>

00:21:21.740 --> 00:21:23.590
There they are!

00:21:24.860 --> 00:21:26.970
It's the Knights-sorcerers!

00:21:29.650 --> 00:21:31.550
Sir Mordred!

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:35.620
Look over here!

00:21:37.380 --> 00:21:39.580
Please look at me!

00:21:39.580 --> 00:21:41.380
Those are the Knights-sorcerers?

00:21:41.380 --> 00:21:42.980
You don't even know them?

00:21:42.980 --> 00:21:44.460
What backwater are you from?

00:21:44.460 --> 00:21:47.110
They're Sir Mordred and Sir Sagramore!

00:21:47.110 --> 00:21:47.990
Huh?

00:21:47.990 --> 00:21:50.560
<i>Mordred and Sagramore.</i>

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:54.280
<i>These two men, popularly known
 as the "Nemesis' nightmare,"</i>

00:21:54.280 --> 00:21:58.000
<i>are the youngest and most promising 
of all the aspiring Knights-sorcerers</i>

00:21:58.000 --> 00:22:00.500
<i>who are still awaiting 
their ordinance ceremony.</i>

00:22:00.500 --> 00:22:04.790
Huh... So taking out Nemesis 
is the Knights-sorcerers' job,

00:22:04.790 --> 00:22:06.750
and they're sort of like apprentices?

00:22:06.750 --> 00:22:08.870
Sir Mordred, you're wonderful!

00:22:08.870 --> 00:22:12.450
Good luck destroying the Nemesis,
 Sir Sagramore!

00:22:12.450 --> 00:22:14.360
Sir Sagramore!

00:22:14.360 --> 00:22:15.890
I just love that cool expression!

00:22:15.890 --> 00:22:19.940
Huh... Sorcerers are actually popular here.

00:22:23.230 --> 00:22:24.060
Huh?!

00:22:24.060 --> 00:22:25.990
Melie?! Doc?!

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:27.510
Why are they here?!

00:22:25.990 --> 00:22:29.990
To Be Continued

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>Next Time</b>

00:24:01.380 --> 00:24:05.630
<i>Seth has finally arrived in the city
 of the Knights-sorcerers,</i>

00:24:06.050 --> 00:24:09.270
<i>but he is denied entrance 
into the castle.</i>

00:24:10.010 --> 00:24:13.910
<i>Left at a loss,
 Seth encounters a strange old man named Myr.</i>

00:24:14.380 --> 00:24:15.740
<i>With his guidance,</i>

00:24:15.740 --> 00:24:20.020
<i>Seth meets Ocoho,
 a girl who aspires to be a Knight-sorcerer.</i>

00:24:20.630 --> 00:24:23.790
<i>Next time on <i>Radiant</i>, 
"The City of Knights."</i>

00:24:21.120 --> 00:24:25.020
<b>The City of Knights 
-Caislean Merlin-</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>I've finally found</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>the rock!</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>Yum!</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>...the rock.</b>

00:24:25.020 --> 00:24:30.250
<b>End</b>
